From 8b3165ce374ebc386329072ae76764414344581f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 77ph <tk@itarragon.net>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:34:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] feat: bind Safe executions inside EntryPoint.handleOps
 (smart-account owners)

Readers that recover a router call from the transaction behind an event
decoded the transaction input strictly as Safe.execTransaction. When the
Safe's owner is a smart account, that transaction is EntryPoint.handleOps:
other operators could not recover our verdict digests, and our own
settlement binding would mark such settlements orphaned.

- marketplace-binding: safeExecutionsOf(publicClient, txHash) returns the
  Safe executions a transaction actually ran: the transaction itself (owner
  EOA), or the Safe calls inside the ERC-7579 execute (single or batch) of
  each UserOperation of an EntryPoint v0.7 handleOps bundle whose
  UserOperationEvent (emitted by that EntryPoint) reports success.
- venue-base verdict.ts (readVerdictSettlement) and operator
  native-base-sepolia-infrastructure.ts (solution settlement binding) use it;
  the direct path keeps its exact behaviour and messages, and more than one
  matching verdict call in one transaction is refused.
- tests: the helper (direct, bundle with a reverted foreign operation,
  EntryPoint-spoofed event, call types); both readers on a handleOps bundle
  (bound when the UserOperation succeeded, refused when it failed); the
  Kernel-owner hermetic loop now also binds its real settlement transaction.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
